menu "OBD2 dashboard"

    config DASH_BIKE_PROFILE
        string "Bike profile (a header in main/bike/profiles/, without .h)"
        default "generic"
        help
            The motorcycle's numbers: rev range, gear ratios, coolant and voltage
            limits, displacement, tank size and tyre pressures. "generic" suits any
            bike; "honda_cb500x" is a complete example. To add yours, copy
            main/bike/profiles/generic.h to main/bike/profiles/<name>.h, edit it and
            enter <name> here. See docs/configure-your-bike.md.

    config DASH_DEMO_DEFAULT
        bool "Start in demo mode (synthetic data, no Bluetooth)"
        default y
        help
            Demo mode plays a synthetic ride, geared to the bike profile, plus staged
            alerts, so every page can be checked on the desk. It can be switched on
            the Status page at any time (saved in NVS); this only sets the value on
            a fresh board.

    config DASH_ADAPTER_NAME
        string "Preferred adapter name (substring, empty = any known ELM327 name)"
        default ""
        help
            Advertised-name filter, e.g. "IOS-Vlink". Empty accepts any adapter that
            advertises a known ELM327 service or name.

    config DASH_PERF_MONITOR
        bool "Show LVGL's FPS / CPU overlay"
        default n

    config DASH_LOG_DEMO
        bool "Write ride logs to the microSD card in demo mode too"
        default n
        help
            Off: only real rides are logged. On is for checking the logger on the desk.

    config DASH_FORMAT_SD_ON_BOOT
        bool "Format the microSD card once at boot (ERASES IT)"
        default n
        help
            Formats the card (FAT32, 32 KB clusters) on the first boot of this firmware build
            and never again for the same build. Leave off: the Status page has a Format
            button behind a confirm.

    config DASH_AUTOTOUR
        bool "Swipe through the pages by itself (desk demo, FPS checks)"
        default n

    config DASH_SCREENSHOTS
        bool "Dump a screenshot of every page over the serial port at boot (development)"
        default n
        select LV_USE_SNAPSHOT
        help
            Shows each page in turn and prints it as base64 RGB565 between SHOT/ENDSHOT lines.
            tools/grab_screens.py turns them into PNGs.

    config DASH_SCREENSHOT_DELAY_S
        int "Seconds after boot before the first screenshot"
        depends on DASH_SCREENSHOTS
        default 0
        help
            The demo ride is under way from about 30 s to 230 s (the demo overheats at
            236 s), so 160 gives screenshots of a bike on the road.

endmenu
